The `max_sum` list stores the maximum sum of non-adjacent elements up to the i-th index of the input array. The base cases are handled for arrays of length 0, 1, and 2. For arrays of length greater than 2, the `max_sum` list is populated using the recurrence relation `max_sum[i] = max(max_sum[i-1], max_sum[i-2] + arr[i])`, which states that the maximum sum of non-adjacent elements up to the i-th index is either the maximum sum up to the (i-1)-th index or the sum of the i-th element and the maximum sum up to the (i-2)-th index. Finally, the last element of the `max_sum` list is returned as the maximum sum of non-adjacent elements.

